<?xml version="1.0"?>
<sdf version="1.9">
  <model name="agriculture_world">
    <static>true</static>

    <!-- Placement. Two transforms are folded into the pose below.
         1. YAW 180deg. Upstream's URDF spawns the mesh with rpy="0 0 pi" to
            align the scene so X+ is east and Y+ is north (ENU), which is the
            convention this world already uses. Keeping it means the farm's
            north is our north.
         2. TRANSLATION +22 +27 -0.25, which puts the flight area on an open
            pad INSIDE the farm rather than beside it.

            Picking that pad needs world-space geometry, and this mesh will
            mislead you if you read it naively: most of its objects are
            INSTANCED, so the raw <float_array> coordinates are local to each
            object and cluster around (0,0). Reading them without walking the
            <visual_scene> node transforms says the farm is 80m wide and dense
            at the origin; walking the transforms says it actually spans
            X -36..115, Y -59..101. A first attempt at this offset was chosen
            from the un-transformed numbers and parked the vehicle at mesh
            x=-40 - past the edge of the mesh, so the farm sat off to one side
            with the star flying over nothing.

            With transforms applied: the buildings cluster around mesh
            (9, 16), the whole scene centres near (39, 21), and mesh (22, 27)
            is a flat open pad - clear of anything above 1.5m out to an 11m
            radius, ground varying only 0.25m. That is well inside the farm
            and next to the built-up area, so the buildings, silos and crop
            rows surround the mission instead of sitting behind it.

            After the 180deg yaw, mesh (22, 27, 0.25) maps to world
            (-22, -27, 0.25), so the model is translated by (+22, +27, -0.25)
            to bring that pad to world (0, 0, 0). The star (radius 6m) and the
            8/18/28m rings then fly over open ground with the farm as
            surrounding scenery rather than as obstacles. -->
    <pose>22 27 -0.25 0 0 3.14159265358979</pose>

    <link name="link">
      <collision name="collision">
        <geometry>
          <mesh><uri>meshes/agriculture_world.dae</uri></mesh>
        </geometry>
        <surface>
          <friction>
            <ode>
              <mu>100</mu>
              <mu2>50</mu2>
            </ode>
          </friction>
        </surface>
      </collision>

      <visual name="visual">
        <geometry>
          <mesh><uri>meshes/agriculture_world.dae</uri></mesh>
        </geometry>
      </visual>
    </link>
  </model>
</sdf>
